From 4dde40b4efe8abc4e62fcde41874172660959418 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:33:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 42/54] TABLE: DXF import and export of ACAD_TABLE

AutoCAD writes ACAD_TABLE to every DXF version in the pre-R2010 form
(example_2000.dxf .. example_2018.dxf, 2000/TS1.dxf): the INSERT part,
then 342 343 11 90 91 92 93-96, the row heights (141) before the column
widths (142), and per cell 171-176, the override flag (177, 91 since
R2007), 178, 145, then the text (1) before R2007 or the value
(301 CELL_VALUE 93 90 1 94 300 302 304 ACVALUE_END) since R2007, with
92 before it. R2010+ adds 280 0 before 342. The TABLECONTENT object is
not needed for the table.

- out_dxf: dxf_ACAD_TABLE writes this, R2010+ tables converted from the
  table content as for R2000 DWG (downconvert_TABLE). The output for
  example_2000/2007/2018.dwg is the AutoCAD DXF of the same drawing,
  except handles and the anonymous block name (separate saves) and, for
  R2018, flag 90 (6, AutoCAD 22) and the 0x40000 cell flag bit, which
  the conversion does not make.
- in_dxf: add_ACAD_TABLE reads it after <100 AcDbTable> into the
  pre-R2010 fields, the cell text from 1 (2/3 chunks) or from the value
  (302, else 1). TABLE is importable again, and no longer written as a
  placeholder from DXF; TABLECONTENT still is.
- Cell and table overrides follow the DWG field order with the DXF codes
  of the spec; no AutoCAD sample has any, so their DXF order is a guess.
  Colors are ACI (0xc3 with the index in the low byte, as the R2000
  samples). 177 is 16-bit: the visibility bits 0x8000-0x20000 are given
  by their groups 285/286/288 and set again on import (without them
  ACadSharp could not read the sample_AC1015 tables), 0x40000 is dropped
  as AutoCAD does (177 is 0 in example_2000.dxf, the DWG cell has it).
- free_TABLE_r2010 also frees the value strings and attribute
  definitions of cells imported from R2010+ DXF.
- dxf.test: tables are written to R2000+ DXF again.

Checked with ACadSharp (~/dwg-oracle roundtrip.py --via-dxf, dwg2dxf ->
dxf2dwg --as r2000): example_2000..2018, sample_AC1015..AC1032 and
2000/TS1 lose no ACAD_TABLE (18 before). Rows, columns, widths, heights,
cell values, merged ranges, position and style of all 18 tables equal
the R2000 files saved by AutoCAD (example_2000.dwg, sample_AC1015.dwg)
and the direct dwgrewrite R2000 output; for R2007 input the DXF way
keeps the cell texts that the direct way loses. AutoCAD's own
example_2000..2018.dxf convert to the same table. ACadSharp's DxfReader
reads the written DXF tables as AutoCAD's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 programs/dxf.test.in |   2 +-
 src/classes.c        |   3 +-
 src/encode.c         |   5 +-
 src/free.c           |  21 +-
 src/in_dxf.c         | 734 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/out_dxf.c        | 404 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 1159 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/programs/dxf.test.in b/programs/dxf.test.in
